================ why this is forced, not an accident ================
1. The empty protocol is admissible (no law fires, nothing is unwarranted,
   no ban is armed, nothing is ungrounded): ADM[{}] = 1.
2. Therefore O({}) = {} for EVERY operator whose fixpoints are the admissible sets.
3. The Kripke-Kleene iteration starts at (BOTTOM, TOP), whose interval is all of L
   and therefore contains {}. So its lower bound is glb O(L) <= O({}) = BOTTOM.
4. Every atom of this instance occurs in some admissible set (union = TOP: true),
   so the upper bound is lub O(L) >= union of Adm = TOP.
   => U_O(BOTTOM,TOP) = (BOTTOM,TOP) and KK = (BOTTOM,TOP), for ANY such O.
This is a theorem about the atlas, not a property of one chosen O.
